# What the deployment leaves out (plan item 1.2, 6 Oct 2026).
#
# /index.html is the whole app in one file: its 3.5MB script and its
# stylesheet inline. The tools that read the engine out of it need it in
# the repository (scanner/scan.mjs, ingest/, syntax.mjs, the harnesses). It is
# not deployed. Vercel serves a file before any rewrite, so a deployed
# index.html would answer / itself, and vercel.json's rewrite of / to
# pages/home.app.html (index.html linked, like every other page) would never
# be reached. /index.html is also a 308 to / (vercel.json redirects, which
# come before the file system).
#
# Only literal paths from the root: build.mjs (vercelIgnore) and serve.mjs
# read this file the same way and refuse anything else.
/index.html

# The NAPIC extract whole (plan item 1.6, the owner's D7, 6 Oct 2026). Every
# benchmark napic-ingest.mjs took, twelve divisions in one 1MB file, and its
# own licence note says bulk export and raw-file download stay disabled until
# JPPH confirms commercial redistribution rights. It stays in the repository
# as the source; build.mjs writes data/napic-h1-2025/<division>.json from it,
# one division a file with only what the area screen shows, and the page asks
# for the one it needs.
/data/napic-h1-2025.json
